{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 140,
    "dDurationMs": 4199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One thing that's astounding about Einstein's\npublications in 1905 is that they spanned"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4339,
    "dDurationMs": 4471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "such a large breadth of physics: after illuminating\nthe quantum nature of light by explaining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8810,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the photoelectric effect in March, in April\nhe turned to something apparently more mundane:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13360,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particles suspended in fluids."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15580,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In particular, if you look at tiny particles\nin water, or dust motes in the air, you'll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19940,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "see that they jitter about in a very odd and\nrandom way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22830,
    "dDurationMs": 4359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, it appears odd and random unless\nyou believe that the air or water itself is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27189,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made up of even smaller particles called atoms\nor molecules, which just bounce off of each"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31499,
    "dDurationMs": 1351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other according to very simple rules."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32850,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is called Brownian motion, despite the\nfact that botanist Brown wasn't the first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37480,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to discover it, and similarly Einstein wan't\nthe first to describe it mathematically…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41420,
    "dDurationMs": 4049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but he did draw the conclusion that the mathematical\ndescription of Brownian motion is evidence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45469,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the existence of atoms even if you can't\nsee them directly, and then he cleverly derived"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49609,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how big atoms should be just based on how\nmuch the Brownian particles move."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53199,
    "dDurationMs": 3751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's like measuring the size of a penguin\njust by looking at how icebergs jiggle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56950,
    "dDurationMs": 13180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Talk about cold and calculating!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
